# /doc — local change log

When the user message is `/doc` or starts with `/doc `:

1. Open `DOC.md` at the repo root (gitignored).
2. Append or revise entries for work done in the current session (or topic named after `/doc`).
3. Use **one line per change** — short, factual, past tense or imperative style.
4. Group entries under a dated section header if starting a new day or topic.
5. Update the `Last updated:` line at the top to today's date.
6. Do not commit `DOC.md`; it is intentionally gitignored.

If `/doc` includes extra text (e.g. `/doc log pipeline`), scope updates to that topic only.
